# Normalize line endings across the team so the bash hooks/scripts keep working everywhere.
# Shell scripts and the renderer MUST stay LF (they run under bash on Linux and Git Bash on
# Windows; CRLF would break shebangs / `bash` execution). .docx are binary.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.log  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.docx binary

# --- Conflict policy (AGENTS.md rule 14): NEVER lose either side's data ---
# The built-in `union` merge driver resolves a conflict by keeping BOTH versions of the conflicting
# hunk (concatenated, no conflict markers) — so no knowledge from either teammate is ever dropped.
# Applied to human-readable DATA only (knowledge, playbooks, reports .md, audit logs, text). It may
# occasionally duplicate a line/heading — that's the "clean it later" case, never a deletion.
*.md  merge=union
*.log merge=union
*.txt merge=union
# Code / config are deliberately NOT union-merged — concatenating both versions would corrupt a
# script or make invalid JSON/YAML. A conflict in these pauses for review (git-sync warns; nothing
# deleted). Resolve keeping both sides.
*.sh   merge=text
*.mjs  merge=text
*.py   merge=text
*.json merge=text
*.yaml merge=text
*.yml  merge=text
